# Inner product `i_nner` (B6, F9): in `A '+ '* i_nner B` the nearest
# operand '* pairs items and '+ reduces them (a right fold, like r_/).
# The last axis of A pairs with the first axis of B, as in APL and J:
# vectors give a scalar (dot product), matrices multiply, and a single
# value extends along the paired axis.
== SOURCE
1 2 3 '+ '* i_nner 4 5 6
(2 2 r_eshape 1 2 3 4) '+ '* i_nner 2 2 r_eshape 5 6 7 8
(2 3 r_eshape r_ange 6) '+ '* i_nner 1 1 1
2 '+ '* i_nner 1 2 3
1 2 3 'm_ax '+ i_nner 3 2 1
"abc" '& '= i_nner "abc"
1 2 3 '- '* i_nner 1 1 1
1 2 3 '+ '= i_nner 1 5 3
